fans and critics alike have already  started to weigh in on Adam warlock's  looks in the Guardians of the Galaxy vol  3 trailer here's how he Stacks up to his  comic book counterpart  the long-awaited debut of the Guardians  of the Galaxy vol 3 movie trailer has  finally come and has already garnered  millions of YouTube views and there are  a lot of revealing bits of the story  packed into just under two minutes  there's a strong hint that many of the  main characters will meet a fatal end  and the introduction of Lila a fan  favorite character from the comics but  the debut of another comic book  character that fans have been waiting  for since Guardians of the Galaxy Vol 2  debuted in 2017 is probably the biggest  reveal that character is none other than  Adam Warlock played by Will Poulter  think I shall call him  Adam  there's a ton of hype for the film as a  whole but the chatter around warlock is  particularly positive many fans are  eager for the emotional payoff they've  been waiting almost six years for what  they may not know however is that  adapting warlock from the comics in a  way that would please moviegoers and  comic book fans alike as a tall ask  thanks to his many rebirths in the  comics Adam Warlock has had more costume  changes than even the most seasoned  X-Men veteran from the brief look we get  it's clear that warlock will be wearing  his red uniform with a skull affixed to  the collar this is the costume he wore  after being resurrected to defeat Thanos  and protect half of all life in the  universe from being blinked out of  existence by The Infinity Gauntlet it  makes sense that the studio would go  with this look since that's also the arc  where he has the most interaction with  nebula Gamora and Drax all of whom will  be returning for Guardians of the Galaxy  Vol 3. so far the vast majority of fans  are in favor of this Choice several  redditor think the makeup has improved  since the last film and although other  commenters didn't see much of a  difference at all they agree it looks  good and fits well with the Sci-Fi tone  of the film but not everyone is as  optimistic even though there's a ton of  praise for warlock's split second  appearance in this appreciation thread  for the trailer one user said I feel  like they could punch up the color on  those costumes a bit but the top comment  from Reddit expressing enthusiasm for  warlock's presence in the trailer has  hundreds of upvotes so far so it's safe  to assume that the look he'll be  sporting in the MCU will go over well  with the majority of audiences those who  have viewed the trailer saw warlock for  no more than a second and in that brief  amount of time all we see is a brief  shot of his face from the shoulders up  as well as him seemingly punching a  downed nebula hard in the head if you  pay close enough attention you can see  the skull decoration on the movie  version of his suit albeit it's muted to  blend in rather than standing up  prominently as it does in the comics  he's also sporting a very powerful soul  German is for him and it does appear as  though he still has his red cape bands  and critics alike are impressed with how  warlock looks in the trailer prominent  movie critic Tessa Smith at Rotten  Tomatoes in a longer tweet about the  overall impression the trailer made on  her said I'm not ready to say goodbye to  these guys but can we talk about how  incredible Adam Warlock looks with the  warm reception warlock has received so  far it would be a surprise if fans ended  up hating him after seeing him make his  big MCU debut in theaters next year  foreign
 

